E('world war i|world war 1|ww1|wwi|first world war|great war', 'The First World War was a global conflict centred on Europe.', 'It lasted from 28 July 1914 to 11 November 1918.',
  'It was sparked by the assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria-Hungary in Sarajevo in June 1914.', 'The Allies, including France, Britain, Russia and later the US, fought the Central Powers, led by Germany and Austria-Hungary.', 'The Western Front became a deadlock of trench warfare.', 'New weapons included machine guns, poison gas, tanks and aircraft.', 'About 9 to 10 million soldiers died.', 'The Treaty of Versailles in 1919 imposed harsh terms on Germany.',
  'It toppled four empires and set the stage for the Second World War.')
E('franz ferdinand|archduke franz ferdinand|assassination of franz ferdinand|gavrilo princip', 'Archduke Franz Ferdinand was heir to the throne of Austria-Hungary; his assassination triggered the First World War.', 'He was shot in Sarajevo on 28 June 1914.',
  'The assassin was Gavrilo Princip, a young Bosnian Serb nationalist.', 'His driver took a wrong turn, stopping right where Princip stood.', 'His wife, Sophie, was killed too.', 'Austria-Hungary declared war on Serbia a month later, and alliances pulled in the other powers.',
  'Two shots in Sarajevo set off one of the deadliest wars in history.')
E('trench warfare|trenches|the somme|battle of the somme', 'Trench warfare defined the Western Front in the First World War.', 'The Battle of the Somme was fought from July to November 1916.',
  'Soldiers lived in muddy trenches separated by a deadly “no man’s land”.', 'On the first day of the Somme, the British army suffered about 57,000 casualties.', 'Over a million men were killed or wounded at the Somme.', 'Tanks were used for the first time there.',
  'The Somme became a symbol of the war’s horror and waste.')
E('treaty of versailles|versailles treaty', 'The Treaty of Versailles was the peace settlement that ended the First World War with Germany.', 'It was signed on 28 June 1919.',
  'Germany had to accept blame for the war.', 'It lost territory, its colonies and most of its military.', 'It had to pay huge reparations.', 'It also created the League of Nations.',
  'Resentment of the treaty helped Hitler rise to power.')
E('russian revolution|october revolution|bolsheviks|bolshevik revolution', 'The Russian Revolution overthrew the tsar and brought the Communist Bolsheviks to power.', 'It happened in 1917, in two stages: February and October.',
  'Tsar Nicholas II abdicated in March 1917.', 'In November (October in Russia’s old calendar) Lenin’s Bolsheviks seized power.', 'A civil war followed until about 1922.', 'The tsar and his family were executed in 1918.', 'The Soviet Union was formed in 1922.',
  'It created the world’s first communist state and shaped the 20th century.')
E('lenin|vladimir lenin', 'Vladimir Lenin was the leader of the Bolshevik Revolution and the founder of the Soviet state.', 'He lived from 1870 to 1924.',
  'He led the October Revolution of 1917.', 'He pulled Russia out of the First World War.', 'His government used violence against opponents during the Civil War.', 'His body is still displayed in a mausoleum in Moscow.',
  'His ideas, called Leninism, shaped communist movements worldwide.')
E('joseph stalin|stalin', 'Joseph Stalin was the dictator of the Soviet Union for nearly three decades.', 'He lived from 1878 to 1953 and held power from the mid-1920s until his death.',
  'He forced rapid industrialisation and the collectivisation of farms.', 'Collectivisation caused famines, including the Holodomor in Ukraine, killing millions.', 'His Great Purge of the late 1930s killed hundreds of thousands, and millions went to Gulag labour camps.', 'The USSR helped defeat Nazi Germany in the Second World War at enormous cost.', 'After the war he built a Soviet bloc in Eastern Europe.',
  'He is remembered as one of the most brutal dictators in history.')
E('great depression|wall street crash|1929 crash', 'The Great Depression was the worst economic downturn of the industrialised world.', 'It began with the Wall Street Crash in October 1929 and lasted through the 1930s.',
  'Stock prices collapsed, and banks failed.', 'In the US, unemployment reached about 25 per cent.', 'It spread worldwide through trade and finance.', 'US President Franklin D. Roosevelt responded with the New Deal.', 'Hardship helped extremist movements rise in Europe.',
  'It reshaped how governments manage economies.')
E('franklin roosevelt|fdr|franklin d roosevelt|new deal', 'Franklin D. Roosevelt was the 32nd US President, who led the country through the Depression and most of the Second World War.', 'He lived from 1882 to 1945 and was president from 1933.',
  'He was the only president elected four times.', 'His New Deal created jobs, banking reforms and Social Security.', 'He had polio and used a wheelchair, which he mostly kept from public view.', 'He said, “The only thing we have to fear is fear itself.”', 'He died in April 1945, weeks before Germany surrendered.',
  'He transformed the role of the US government.')
E('world war ii|world war 2|ww2|wwii|second world war', 'The Second World War was the deadliest conflict in human history.', 'It lasted from 1 September 1939 to 2 September 1945.',
  'It began when Germany invaded Poland.', 'The Allies, mainly Britain, the Soviet Union, the US and China, fought the Axis: Germany, Italy and Japan.', 'Nazi Germany conquered much of Europe by 1941.', 'Japan’s attack on Pearl Harbor in December 1941 brought the US into the war.', 'An estimated 70 to 85 million people died, most of them civilians.', 'Germany surrendered in May 1945, and Japan in September after the atomic bombings.',
  'It led to the United Nations, the Cold War and decolonisation.')
E('adolf hitler|hitler|nazi|nazis|nazi germany|third reich', 'Adolf Hitler was the dictator of Nazi Germany, responsible for the Second World War in Europe and the Holocaust.', 'He lived from 1889 to 1945 and ruled Germany from 1933.',
  'He was born in Austria and fought in the First World War.', 'He led the Nazi Party, which spread racist, antisemitic and nationalist ideas.', 'He became chancellor in January 1933 and quickly made himself dictator.', 'He invaded Poland in 1939, starting the war.', 'His regime murdered six million Jews and millions of others.', 'He took his own life in a Berlin bunker in April 1945.',
  'His name is a byword for evil, and the horrors of his regime led to modern human rights laws.')
E('holocaust|the holocaust|shoah|auschwitz', 'The Holocaust was the genocide of European Jews by Nazi Germany and its collaborators.', 'It took place from 1941 to 1945, after years of persecution from 1933.',
  'About six million Jews were murdered, around two-thirds of Europe’s Jewish population.', 'Roma, disabled people, Poles, Soviet prisoners, gay men and others were also killed.', 'Victims were shot in mass killings or murdered in death camps.', 'Auschwitz-Birkenau, in occupied Poland, was the largest camp; over a million people died there.', 'Allied troops liberated the camps in 1945.', 'Nazi leaders were tried at Nuremberg.',
  'It is remembered so that such crimes are never repeated: “Never again”.')
E('anne frank', 'Anne Frank was a Jewish girl whose wartime diary became one of the most famous books in the world.', 'She lived from 1929 to 1945.',
  'Her family hid from the Nazis in a secret annex in Amsterdam for over two years.', 'She wrote her diary from 1942 to 1944.', 'The family was discovered and deported in August 1944.', 'She died at Bergen-Belsen concentration camp, aged 15.', 'Her father, Otto, survived and published her diary in 1947.',
  'Her diary puts a human face on the Holocaust for millions of readers.')
E('winston churchill|churchill', 'Winston Churchill was Britain’s Prime Minister during most of the Second World War.', 'He lived from 1874 to 1965 and was PM from 1940 to 1945 and 1951 to 1955.',
  'He became PM in May 1940, as Germany invaded France.', 'His speeches rallied Britain: “We shall fight on the beaches” and “their finest hour”.', 'He worked closely with Roosevelt and, uneasily, Stalin.', 'He won the Nobel Prize in Literature in 1953.', 'His record on empire and some wartime decisions remain controversial.',
  'He is remembered as a great wartime leader.')
E('battle of britain', 'The Battle of Britain was an air campaign in which the RAF defended Britain against the German Luftwaffe.', 'It was fought from July to October 1940.',
  'Germany needed control of the skies to invade Britain.', 'Radar gave the RAF a vital advantage.', 'Pilots came from many countries, including Poland and Czechoslovakia.', 'Churchill said, “Never was so much owed by so many to so few.”',
  'It was Hitler’s first major defeat.')
E('pearl harbor|pearl harbour', 'Pearl Harbor is a US naval base in Hawaii that Japan attacked by surprise.', 'The attack came on 7 December 1941.',
  'Japanese aircraft struck the US Pacific Fleet.', 'More than 2,400 Americans were killed.', 'Eight battleships were damaged or sunk, though US aircraft carriers were at sea.', 'Roosevelt called it “a date which will live in infamy”.',
  'It brought the United States into the Second World War.')
E('d-day|d day|normandy landings|operation overlord', 'D-Day was the Allied invasion of Nazi-occupied France.', 'It took place on 6 June 1944, in Normandy.',
  'It was the largest seaborne invasion in history.', 'About 156,000 Allied troops landed on five beaches: Utah, Omaha, Gold, Juno and Sword.', 'It was led by US General Dwight Eisenhower.', 'Elaborate deception made Germany expect the landing elsewhere.', 'By August, Paris was liberated.',
  'It opened a second front in Europe and sped Germany’s defeat.')
E('stalingrad|battle of stalingrad', 'The Battle of Stalingrad was a turning point on the Eastern Front.', 'It lasted from August 1942 to February 1943.',
  'German forces fought their way into the city, street by street.', 'A Soviet counter-attack encircled the German Sixth Army.', 'Around 90,000 Germans surrendered.', 'Total casualties are estimated at nearly two million.',
  'After Stalingrad, Germany was largely on the retreat in the east.')
E('hiroshima|nagasaki|atomic bomb|atomic bombings', 'The US dropped atomic bombs on the Japanese cities of Hiroshima and Nagasaki.', 'They were dropped on 6 and 9 August 1945.',
  'Hiroshima was hit by a bomb called “Little Boy”, Nagasaki by “Fat Man”.', 'Together they killed an estimated 110,000 to 210,000 people.', 'Many survivors, called hibakusha, suffered radiation illness.', 'Japan announced its surrender on 15 August 1945.',
  'They are the only nuclear weapons ever used in war, and they shaped the nuclear age.')
E('manhattan project|oppenheimer|robert oppenheimer', 'The Manhattan Project was the secret US-led program that built the first atomic bombs.', 'It ran from 1942 to 1946.',
  'J. Robert Oppenheimer led the Los Alamos laboratory in New Mexico.', 'Britain and Canada contributed.', 'The first test, Trinity, took place on 16 July 1945.', 'Oppenheimer later recalled the line, “Now I am become Death, the destroyer of worlds.”',
  'It began the nuclear age.')
E('nuremberg trials', 'The Nuremberg trials prosecuted leaders of Nazi Germany for war crimes.', 'The main trial ran from 1945 to 1946.',
  'Twenty-four leading Nazis were charged.', 'Twelve were sentenced to death.', 'They established crimes against humanity as an international legal idea.',
  'They became a foundation of international criminal law.')
E('united nations|un', 'The United Nations is an international organisation that promotes peace and cooperation.', 'It was founded on 24 October 1945.',
  'It replaced the failed League of Nations.', 'It has 193 member states.', 'Its Security Council has five permanent members with vetoes: the US, UK, France, Russia and China.', 'Its headquarters are in New York.', 'The Universal Declaration of Human Rights was adopted in 1948.',
  'It remains the main forum for global diplomacy.')
E('cold war', 'The Cold War was a long rivalry between the United States and the Soviet Union.', 'It lasted from about 1947 to 1991.',
  'It was “cold” because the two never fought each other directly.', 'They competed through an arms race, the Space Race and proxy wars.', 'NATO and the Warsaw Pact were rival military alliances.', 'The Cuban Missile Crisis of 1962 brought the world close to nuclear war.', 'The Berlin Wall fell in 1989.', 'The Soviet Union dissolved in December 1991.',
  'It shaped world politics for nearly half a century.')
E('berlin wall|fall of the berlin wall', 'The Berlin Wall divided communist East Berlin from West Berlin.', 'It stood from 13 August 1961 to 9 November 1989.',
  'East Germany built it to stop people fleeing west.', 'At least 140 people died trying to cross it.', 'US President Reagan said in 1987, “Mr Gorbachev, tear down this wall!”', 'It opened after an East German official mistakenly announced that border crossings were open immediately.', 'Germany was reunified on 3 October 1990.',
  'Its fall became a symbol of the end of the Cold War.')
E('cuban missile crisis', 'The Cuban Missile Crisis was a confrontation that brought the US and USSR close to nuclear war.', 'It lasted thirteen days in October 1962.',
  'US spy planes found Soviet nuclear missiles in Cuba.', 'President Kennedy ordered a naval “quarantine” of Cuba.', 'Soviet leader Khrushchev agreed to remove the missiles.', 'Secretly, the US agreed to remove its missiles from Turkey.', 'A hotline between Washington and Moscow was set up afterwards.',
  'It is often called the closest the world has come to nuclear war.')
E('korean war', 'The Korean War was fought between North and South Korea, with international involvement.', 'It lasted from 1950 to 1953.',
  'North Korea invaded the South in June 1950.', 'A UN force led by the US defended the South.', 'China joined on the North’s side.', 'It ended in an armistice, not a peace treaty.',
  'Korea remains divided today.')
E('vietnam war', 'The Vietnam War was fought between communist North Vietnam and South Vietnam, which the US supported.', 'US involvement grew from the 1950s; combat troops fought from 1965 to 1973.',
  'The North was backed by the USSR and China.', 'Guerrilla fighters, the Viet Cong, fought in the South.', 'The Tet Offensive in 1968 shocked the American public.', 'Large anti-war protests took place in the US.', 'Saigon fell to the North in April 1975.', 'Millions of Vietnamese died.',
  'It deeply shaped American politics and its view of war.')
E('mikhail gorbachev|gorbachev', 'Mikhail Gorbachev was the last leader of the Soviet Union.', 'He lived from 1931 to 2022 and led the USSR from 1985 to 1991.',
  'He introduced glasnost, “openness”, and perestroika, “restructuring”.', 'He signed arms reduction treaties with the US.', 'He did not use force to stop Eastern Europe leaving communism in 1989.', 'He won the Nobel Peace Prize in 1990.',
  'He is praised abroad for ending the Cold War, but viewed more critically in Russia.')
